0,Haitian Vodoun Culture Language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haitian_Vodoun_Culture_Language,"October 10, 2024 - Haitian Vodoun Culture Language (known as Langay and Langaj; literally ""language"") is a specialized vocabulary used in Haiti for religion, song, and dance purposes.",Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
1,Haitian Vodou - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haitian_Vodou,"1 week ago - Some scholars prefer the spellings Vodoun, Voudoun, or Vodun, while in French the spellings vaudou ... also appear. The spelling Voodoo, once common, is now generally avoided by practitioners and scholars when referring to the Haitian religion. This is both to avoid confusion with Louisiana Voodoo, a related but distinct tradition, and to distinguish it from the negative connotations that the term Voodoo has in Western popular culture...",Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
