3,Haitian Vodoun Culture Language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/haitian_vodoun_culture_language,"The sacred ritual language of Haitian Vodou, known as langaj, originated from the linguistic traditions of West and Central African ethnic groups, primarily the Fon from Dahomey (modern Benin), Yoruba from Nigeria and surrounding areas, and Kongo peoples from Central-West Africa.",Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
