5,"Audio Recording, Haiti, Folk Music | Library of Congress",https://www.loc.gov/audio/?fa=location:haiti|subject:folk+music&c=25&all=true&st=list,"Alan Lomax Haiti collection Catalog Record Only Collection of field recordings of Haitian music and spoken word, including dance music, songs, Vodou ceremonies and drumming, children's games and songs, stories, and interviews.",Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
6,Haitian voodoo vodou haitien - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLHbQsjZ_OfAMkm9PJdENr5OnFfiyzXGCF,"Listen to Haitian voodoo vodou haitien on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
7,Haitian Vodoun Culture Language - Lexvo - Finto.fi,https://finto.fi/lexvo/en/page/hvc,"Haitian Vodoun Culture Language is an unclassified language used in Haiti. It is also known as Langay and Langaj (meaning literally ""language""). This language is used for religion, song, and dance purposes (it is used as a second language only).",Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
8,"Haitian Vodoun Culture Language Language (HVC) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/hvc/,Haitian Vodoun Culture Language is a language of Haiti that is used only as a second language and has no ethnic community. It is an unclassified language. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
9,Rhythms of Rapture: Sacred Musics of Haitian Vodou | Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/rhythms-of-rapture-sacred-musics-of-haitian-vodou/caribbean-world/music/album/smithsonian,"Features recent innovations and traditional roots of this potent music. Cuts from live Vodou ceremonies are juxtaposed with performances by well-known Haitian artists, such as Boukman Experyans, RaRa Machine, Boukan Ginen and RAM.",Haitian Vodoun Culture Language,Unclassified
